---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import SEO from '../components/SEO.astro';
import ForwardLink from '../components/ForwardLink.astro';

const pageTitle = 'Model Workbench';
const pageDescription =
  'Notes from the field building with AI: short practical notes on models, CADE, AI-assisted development, and human judgment.';
---

<PageLayout>
  <SEO
    slot="head"
    title={pageTitle}
    description={pageDescription}
    type="website"
  />

  <section class="workbench-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Model Workbench</p>
    <h1>Notes from the field building with AI.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      This is the place for short notes about how I actually use models: not as a magic answer machine, but as a workbench for thinking, drafting, testing, and building.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="workbench-entries" aria-label="Workbench notes">
    <p class="eyebrow">Notes</p>
    <article class="workbench-entry">
      <header class="entry-header">
        <time class="entry-date" datetime="2026-05-31">May 31, 2026</time>
        <h2>My AI Stack Is a Workbench</h2>
      </header>
      <div class="entry-body">
        <p>I don't have a favorite model. I have a workbench.</p>
        <p>Each model has a job.</p>
        <p>Claude Code is where I start when the work is still fuzzy — discovery, design, specs, audits. Codex is where I hand a spec when I want something built fast. Gemini handles deep research when I need a wide pass across a topic. NotebookLM is for working inside source material once I have it. Local models like Qwen or Hermes run on a Mac mini for lightweight tasks when I want to save tokens.</p>
        <p>The point isn't to collect tools. The point is knowing what each one is actually good for.</p>
        <p>That only comes from use. Gemini can loop. Claude Code is strong but expensive — session limits matter. Codex builds fast, but I don't trust it for design work the way I trust Claude Code. Those aren't complaints. They're operating facts.</p>
        <p>My rule: no model owns the final product.</p>
        <p>The models draft, research, build, audit, and refactor. I make the decisions — structure, direction, quality. I steer. I decide when it's right.</p>
        <p>That matters because models are persuasive. Without thread discipline, you can spend hours chasing the next recommendation. Manage tokens. Watch for drift. Return to the original intent.</p>
        <p>The workbench is valuable not because of the list of tools. It's valuable because you know which tool belongs where, when to switch, and when to stop listening.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="workbench-cta">
    <div>
      <h2>Back to the work</h2>
      <p>
        The notes are the workshop. CADE is the proof that the workshop can produce something usable.
      </p>
    </div>
    <ForwardLink href="/projects/cade" text="Read the CADE case study" />
  </section>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .workbench-hero {
    padding: 2rem 0 3rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .workbench-hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 8vw, 5.25rem);
    line-height: 0.98;
    letter-spacing: -0.06em;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .lead {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 2vw, 1.35rem);
    line-height: 1.65;
    max-width: 68ch;
  }

  .workbench-entries {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .workbench-entries > .eyebrow {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .workbench-entry {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 1.25rem;
    background: var(--color-bg-elevated);
    padding: 2rem;
  }

  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .entry-date {
    display: block;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .entry-header h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 4vw, 2.4rem);
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .entry-body p {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .entry-body p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .workbench-cta {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 1.25rem;
    background: var(--color-bg-elevated);
    padding: 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .workbench-cta h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 4vw, 2.6rem);
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .workbench-cta p {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .workbench-cta {
      align-items: flex-start;
      flex-direction: column;
    }
  }
</style>
